course: dictionary
lesson: 2232
title: Cowardice and fear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cowardice is a noun. It means a lack of courage: being too afraid to do what is right or what is needed. Its opposite is bravery. You can tell its meaning from the sentences around it.
explain: «Hiding behind a cushion or switching off halfway is a sensible choice, not cowardice.» The word not tells you these actions are not cowardice, so cowardice must be something different. The next part, «being brave means doing what is right for you, not proving something», gives the clue: cowardice is about not doing what is right.
explain: Feeling afraid is not the same as cowardice. «Staying down and not fighting back when shoved is not cowardice; it can stop a fight getting bigger.» Cowardice happens when fear stops you doing what is right, not when you are simply scared.
fact: Cowardice means a lack of courage: being too afraid to do what is right or needed.
fact: Cowardice can also mean a shameful act done because of fear.
fact: Cowardice is uncountable, so you do not add an s to make it plural.
fact: Phrases to remember: «an act of cowardice» and «accuse of cowardice».
fact: Feeling fear is normal. Cowardice happens when fear stops you doing what is right.
exercise: What does cowardice mean? | *Being too afraid to do what is right or what is needed | Being loud and proud in front of others | Being very clever at hiding | Being tired after a long day
exercise: Which phrase from the lessons describes a shameful act done because of fear? | an act of kindness | a brave reply | a sensible choice | *an act of cowardice
exercise: «Staying down and not fighting back when shoved is not cowardice; it can stop a fight getting bigger.» Why is this not cowardice? | *It can stop a fight getting bigger | It is always the bravest thing to do | It shows you are afraid of everyone | It means you want to fight
test: Is feeling afraid the same as cowardice? | No, because cowardice is only about being loud | Yes, always | Yes, if you are small | *No, cowardice is letting fear stop you doing what is right
test: Which word is the opposite of cowardice? | Laziness | Shyness | *Bravery | Tiredness
exam: Which sentence shows cowardice correctly? | He stood up for his friend and told the bully to stop. | He read a book about dinosaurs. | He laughed at the clouds in the sky. | *He let his friend be bullied because he was too scared to speak up.
